IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc6-builders`

-- ccc6-morals.l4 -- s 163 (Obscene materials), s 167 (Immoral theatrical performance), s 168 (Mailing obscene matter) and s 169 (Punishment for ss 163, 165, 167 and 168).
-- "obscene", "indecent", "immoral", "scurrilous" and "disgusting" are left to the court by the text (apart from s 163(8)'s deeming); each is a plain input.
-- The punishment of the offences of ss 163, 167 and 168 is not in those sections but in s 169, so the punishment functions are s 169's. (The summary-conviction limb of s 169 states no penalty: the penalty of s 787(1) is an input.)

§ `s 163 Obscene materials`

DECLARE `s 163(1) what the person did` IS ONE OF
    `s 163(1) makes`
    `s 163(1) prints`
    `s 163(1) publishes`
    `s 163(1) distributes`
    `s 163(1) circulates`
    `s 163(1) has in their possession for the purpose of publication, distribution or circulation`
    `s 163(1) none of those`

-- src:3210 | Obscene materials
-- src:3211 | 163 (1) Every person commits an offence who makes, prints, publishes, distributes, circulates or has in their possession for the purpose of publication, distribution or circulation any obscene written matter, picture, model, phonograph record or any other obscene thing.
@ref Criminal Code s 163(1) (src:3210-3211)
GIVEN `what the person did` IS A `s 163(1) what the person did`
      `the thing is an obscene written matter, picture, model, phonograph record or other obscene thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 163(1) the conduct is the offence of making or publishing obscene matter` MEANS
    IF    NOT (`what the person did` EQUALS `s 163(1) none of those`)
      AND `the thing is an obscene written matter, picture, model, phonograph record or other obscene thing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person commits an offence who makes, prints, publishes, distributes, circulates or has in their possession for the purpose of publication, distribution or circulation any obscene written matter, picture, model, phonograph record or any other obscene thing"

DECLARE `s 163(2) what the person did` IS ONE OF
    `s 163(2)(a) sells`
    `s 163(2)(a) exposes to public view`
    `s 163(2)(a) has in their possession for that purpose`
    `s 163(2)(b) publicly exhibits a disgusting object`
    `s 163(2)(b) publicly exhibits an indecent show`
    `s 163(2) none of those`

-- src:3212 | Idem
-- src:3213 | (2) Every person commits an offence who knowingly, without lawful justification or excuse,
-- src:3214 | (a) sells, exposes to public view or has in their possession for that purpose any obscene written matter, picture, model, phonograph record or any other obscene thing; or
-- src:3215 | (b) publicly exhibits a disgusting object or an indecent show.
-- src:3216 | (c) and (d) [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 11]
@ref Criminal Code s 163(2) (src:3212-3216)
GIVEN `the person acted knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acted without lawful justification or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the person did` IS A `s 163(2) what the person did`
      `the thing is an obscene written matter, picture, model, phonograph record or other obscene thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 163(2) the conduct is the offence of selling obscene matter or exhibiting an indecent show` MEANS
    IF    `the person acted knowingly`
      AND `the person acted without lawful justification or excuse`
      AND (   (   (   `what the person did` EQUALS `s 163(2)(a) sells`
                   OR `what the person did` EQUALS `s 163(2)(a) exposes to public view`
                   OR `what the person did` EQUALS `s 163(2)(a) has in their possession for that purpose`)
              AND `the thing is an obscene written matter, picture, model, phonograph record or other obscene thing`)
           OR `what the person did` EQUALS `s 163(2)(b) publicly exhibits a disgusting object`
           OR `what the person did` EQUALS `s 163(2)(b) publicly exhibits an indecent show`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person commits an offence who knowingly, without lawful justification or excuse, (a) sells, exposes to public view or has in their possession for that purpose any obscene written matter, picture, model, phonograph record or any other obscene thing; or (b) publicly exhibits a disgusting object or an indecent show"

-- src:3217 | Defence of public good
-- src:3218 | (3) No person shall be convicted of an offence under this section if the public good was served by the acts that are alleged to constitute the offence and if the acts alleged did not extend beyond what served the public good.
@ref Criminal Code s 163(3) (src:3217-3218)
GIVEN `the public good was served by the acts that are alleged to constitute the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the acts alleged did not extend beyond what served the public good` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 163(3) section 163 gives a defence of public good` MEANS
    IF `the public good was served by the acts that are alleged to constitute the offence` AND `the acts alleged did not extend beyond what served the public good`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be convicted of an offence under this section if the public good was served by the acts that are alleged to constitute the offence and if the acts alleged did not extend beyond what served the public good"

DECLARE `s 163(4) the question` IS ONE OF
    `s 163(4) whether an act served the public good`
    `s 163(4) whether there is evidence that the act alleged went beyond what served the public good`
    `s 163(4) whether the acts did or did not extend beyond what served the public good`
    `s 163(4) another question`

-- src:3219 | Question of law and question of fact
-- src:3220 | (4) For the purposes of this section, it is a question of law whether an act served the public good and whether there is evidence that the act alleged went beyond what served the public good, but it is a question of fact whether the acts did or did not extend beyond what served the public good.
@ref Criminal Code s 163(4) (src:3219-3220)
GIVEN question IS A `s 163(4) the question`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 163(4) the question is a question of law` MEANS
    CONSIDER question
    WHEN `s 163(4) whether an act served the public good` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 163(4) whether there is evidence that the act alleged went beyond what served the public good` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 163(4) whether the acts did or did not extend beyond what served the public good` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but it is a question of fact whether the acts did or did not extend beyond what served the public good"
    WHEN `s 163(4) another question` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of this section, it is a question of law whether an act served the public good and whether there is evidence that the act alleged went beyond what served the public good"

-- src:3221 | Motives irrelevant
-- src:3222 | (5) For the purposes of this section, the motives of an accused are irrelevant.
@ref Criminal Code s 163(5) (src:3221-3222)
GIVEN `the matter is the motives of an accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 163(5) the motives of an accused are relevant` MEANS
    IF `the matter is the motives of an accused`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the motives of an accused are irrelevant"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (5) says nothing of any matter but the accused's motives

-- (8) "any publication a dominant characteristic of which is the undue exploitation of sex, or of sex and any one or more of the following subjects, namely, crime, horror, cruelty and violence, shall be deemed to be obscene."
-- A deeming rule: a publication it does not name is NOT COVERED (the text does not say such a publication is not obscene).
-- src:3225 | Obscene publication
-- src:3226 | (8) For the purposes of this Act, any publication a dominant characteristic of which is the undue exploitation of sex, or of sex and any one or more of the following subjects, namely, crime, horror, cruelty and violence, shall be deemed to be obscene.
@ref Criminal Code s 163(8) (src:3225-3226)
GIVEN `a dominant characteristic of the publication is the undue exploitation of sex` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undue exploitation is of sex alone, or of sex and one or more of crime, horror, cruelty and violence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 163(8) the publication is deemed to be obscene` MEANS
    IF `a dominant characteristic of the publication is the undue exploitation of sex` AND `the undue exploitation is of sex alone, or of sex and one or more of crime, horror, cruelty and violence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any publication a dominant characteristic of which is the undue exploitation of sex, or of sex and any one or more of the following subjects, namely, crime, horror, cruelty and violence, shall be deemed to be obscene"

§ `s 167 Immoral theatrical performance`

DECLARE `s 167(1) what the person did` IS ONE OF
    `s 167(1) presents`
    `s 167(1) gives`
    `s 167(1) allows to be presented or given`
    `s 167(1) none of those`

-- src:3364 | Immoral theatrical performance
-- src:3365 | 167 (1) Every one commits an offence who, being the lessee, manager, agent or person in charge of a theatre, presents or gives or allows to be presented or given therein an immoral, indecent or obscene performance, entertainment or representation.
@ref Criminal Code s 167(1) (src:3364-3365)
GIVEN `the person is the lessee, manager, agent or person in charge of the place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 150 theatre: the place is a theatre` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `what the person did` IS A `s 167(1) what the person did`
      `the performance, entertainment or representation is immoral, indecent or obscene` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167(1) the conduct is the offence of presenting an immoral theatrical performance` MEANS
    IF    `the person is the lessee, manager, agent or person in charge of the place`
      AND `s 150 theatre: the place is a theatre` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND NOT (`what the person did` EQUALS `s 167(1) none of those`)
      AND `the performance, entertainment or representation is immoral, indecent or obscene`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one commits an offence who, being the lessee, manager, agent or person in charge of a theatre, presents or gives or allows to be presented or given therein an immoral, indecent or obscene performance, entertainment or representation"

-- src:3366 | Person taking part
-- src:3367 | (2) Every one commits an offence who takes part or appears as an actor, a performer or an assistant in any capacity, in an immoral, indecent or obscene performance, entertainment or representation in a theatre.
@ref Criminal Code s 167(2) (src:3366-3367)
GIVEN `the person takes part or appears as an actor, a performer or an assistant in any capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the performance, entertainment or representation is immoral, indecent or obscene` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 150 theatre: the place is a theatre` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167(2) the conduct is the offence of taking part in an immoral theatrical performance` MEANS
    IF    `the person takes part or appears as an actor, a performer or an assistant in any capacity`
      AND `the performance, entertainment or representation is immoral, indecent or obscene`
      AND `s 150 theatre: the place is a theatre` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one commits an offence who takes part or appears as an actor, a performer or an assistant in any capacity, in an immoral, indecent or obscene performance, entertainment or representation in a theatre"

§ `s 168 Mailing obscene matter`

-- src:3368 | Mailing obscene matter
-- src:3369 | 168 (1) Every one commits an offence who makes use of the mails for the purpose of transmitting or delivering anything that is obscene, indecent, immoral or scurrilous.
@ref Criminal Code s 168(1) (src:3368-3369)
GIVEN `the person made use of the mails` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was for the purpose of transmitting or delivering something` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is obscene, indecent, immoral or scurrilous` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(1) the conduct is the offence of mailing obscene matter` MEANS
    IF    `the person made use of the mails`
      AND `it was for the purpose of transmitting or delivering something`
      AND `the thing is obscene, indecent, immoral or scurrilous`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one commits an offence who makes use of the mails for the purpose of transmitting or delivering anything that is obscene, indecent, immoral or scurrilous"

-- (2) "Subsection (1) does not apply to a person who (a) ... (b) ... or (c) ...": a flat negative. JUST FALSE for the person who falls in one of the four limbs; NOTHING for any other person (the subsection is silent about them).
-- src:3370 | Exceptions
-- src:3371 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a person who
-- src:3372 | (a) prints or publishes any matter for use in connection with any judicial proceedings or communicates it to persons who are concerned in the proceedings;
-- src:3373 | (b) prints or publishes a notice or report under the direction of a court; or
-- src:3374 | (c) prints or publishes any matter
-- src:3375 | (i) in a volume or part of a genuine series of law reports that does not form part of any other publication and consists solely of reports of proceedings in courts of law, or
-- src:3376 | (ii) in a publication of a technical character that is intended, in good faith, for circulation among members of the legal or medical profession.
@ref Criminal Code s 168(2) (src:3370-3376)
GIVEN `the person prints or publishes any matter for use in connection with any judicial proceedings or communicates it to persons who are concerned in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person prints or publishes a notice or report under the direction of a court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person prints or publishes the matter in a volume or part of a genuine series of law reports that does not form part of any other publication and consists solely of reports of proceedings in courts of law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person prints or publishes the matter in a publication of a technical character that is intended, in good faith, for circulation among members of the legal or medical profession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168(2) subsection (1) applies to the person` MEANS
    IF    `the person prints or publishes any matter for use in connection with any judicial proceedings or communicates it to persons who are concerned in the proceedings`
       OR `the person prints or publishes a notice or report under the direction of a court`
       OR `the person prints or publishes the matter in a volume or part of a genuine series of law reports that does not form part of any other publication and consists solely of reports of proceedings in courts of law`
       OR `the person prints or publishes the matter in a publication of a technical character that is intended, in good faith, for circulation among members of the legal or medical profession`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to a person who (a) prints or publishes any matter for use in connection with any judicial proceedings or communicates it to persons who are concerned in the proceedings; (b) prints or publishes a notice or report under the direction of a court; or (c) prints or publishes any matter"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply to a person who (a) ... (b) ... or (c)"

§ `s 169 Punishment`

-- "Every one who commits an offence under section 163, 165, 167 or 168": section 165 is shown repealed in this text (2018, c. 29, s. 13), but it is still named here (finding 5 of NOTES.md).
-- src:3377 | Punishment
-- src:3378 | 169 Every one who commits an offence under section 163, 165, 167 or 168 is guilty of
-- src:3379 | (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years; or
-- src:3380 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 169 (src:3377-3380)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 169 the offence is one under section 163, 165, 167 or 168` MEANS
       `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 163
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 165
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 167
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence charged` 168

@ref Criminal Code s 169(a) (src:3379)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 169(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 169(b) (src:3380)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 169(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `ss 150 to 182 the punishment on summary conviction that s 787(1) fixes` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 169 (src:3378-3380)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 169 the class of an offence under section 163, 165, 167 or 168` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
